Package: ctOWAS
Type: Package
Title: Cell-Type-Level Omics-Wide Association Studies
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Sinan",
           family = "Zhu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "sinan.zhu@u.duke.nus.edu"),
    person(given = "Xiaoyu",
           family = "Song",
           role = "ths",
           email = "song.xiaoyu@duke-nus.edu.sg"))
Description: Performs cell-type-level omics-wide association studies (OWAS)
    for molecular traits measured in bulk tissue, such as gene expression or
    protein abundance. Bulk molecular traits are modelled as a mixture of K
    cell types, so that genetic prediction weights can be estimated separately
    for each cell type. The package provides tools to (1) estimate sample-level
    cell-type fractions from xCell enrichment scores, bulk expression and
    marker genes; (2) train cell-type-specific elastic-net prediction models
    with split-sample stability screening; and (3) test cell-type-specific and
    joint associations using GWAS summary statistics and a linkage
    disequilibrium reference panel, combining p-values across cell types with
    the aggregated Cauchy association test (ACAT). The method extends MiXcan
    to more than two cell types.
URL: https://github.com/songxiaoyu/ctOWAS
